{"case_id":"T8085","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input-boundary semantics"],"confidence":93,"affected_functions":["spng_decoded_image_size"],"reason":"H0 invokes the changed API and varies fmt, but its fixed spng_set_image_limits(ctx, 200000, 200000) configuration excludes large IHDR width/height combinations needed to meaningfully exercise the refactored SIZE_MAX overflow checks. The later out_size limit does not require this early restriction because it is applied after spng_decoded_image_size().","evidence":["S1 changes spng_decoded_image_size() to select bytes_per_pixel and use unified checks against SIZE_MAX before multiplying width, bytes_per_pixel, and height.","H0 calls spng_set_image_limits(ctx, 200000, 200000) before spng_decoded_image_size(ctx, fmt, &out_size), bounding both dimensions parsed by read_chunks().","H0 already derives fmt from data[1] & 0x7F, so SPNG_FMT_RGBA8, SPNG_FMT_RGBA16, SPNG_FMT_RGB8, and invalid-format handling are addressable; the visible omission is the extreme-dimension arithmetic surface.","H0 checks out_size > 80000000 only after spng_decoded_image_size(), so a size-calculation-only path could test overflow results without allocating or decoding large images."],"recommended_action":"Add a size-focused harness path that invokes spng_decoded_image_size() for all three supported formats with substantially relaxed image limits and extreme IHDR dimension combinations, then stops before malloc/spng_decode_image; retain the existing limits for the allocation-and-decode path."}
